    {
      "id": 482335,
      "username": "volkswagner",
      "name": "volkswagner",
      "created_at": "2025-09-27T11:58:44.886Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thank you <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/daizymodi\">@DaizyModi</a>, you are correct. I meant to say Tax Rules.</p>\n<p>According to the <a href=\"https://docs.frappe.io/erpnext/user/manual/en/delete_company_transactions\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">instructions</a> the <code>Transaction Deletion Record</code> is to be used for the configuration and is editable. In ERPNext v14.56.0 this doctype is editable, but it’s still unlear if/when it’s used if the user manually creates one.</p>\n<p>The instructions are unclear, and a custom app should not be required to request a core doctype’s table not be deleted when clearing transactions, especially if the instructions indicate otherwise.</p>",
